@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Adapt layout across breakpoints and orientation change
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "Component stylesheets and tokens.scss" as css
  participant "TodoPageComponent" as page
  participant "TodoComposerComponent" as composer
  participant "TodoItemComponent" as item
end box
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoStore" as store
end box
user -> user : Type "Buy oat" in the composer and start editing a task title
user -> css : Rotate the device or resize the window (viewport width changes)
css -> css : Re-evaluate media queries built from the $breakpoint-* Sass variables (L2-027)
alt XS below 576 px
  css -> page : Full width column with 16 px side gutters (L2-027)
  css -> page : Header ring 48 px and filter control full width (L2-027)
else SM from 576 px
  css -> page : Full width column up to 560 px, centred, 16 px gutters (L2-027)
  css -> page : Header ring 56 px
else MD from 768 px
  css -> page : 640 px centred column, list on raised rounded surface (L2-027)
else LG and XL from 992 px
  css -> page : 640 px centred column offset 8vh from the top, no stretch (L2-027)
end
css -> item : Wrap long title and grow the row, controls never overlap text (L2-027)
css -> page : No horizontal page scroll from 320 px to 1920 px (L2-027)
note over composer, item
  No component handles a resize event.
  Angular does not re-create the components,
  so the composer text and the edit field are kept (L2-028).
end note
composer --> user : Composer still contains "Buy oat" (L2-028)
page -> store : Read editingId (unchanged)
store --> page : Same editingId
item --> user : Edit field still open with its draft text (L2-028)
@enduml
